<decisions #integrate-embedded-ai-effect-provider apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { version = "1" } (
  <decision #track.effects.dispatch_boundary { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
    <question ?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BW>
    Where should AI workflow effects execute?
    </?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BW>
    <answer ?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BX>
    Effects execute through a programmable embedded provider injected into runtime context, not through an external CLI bridge.
    </?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BX>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BY>
    This keeps the flow library usable as a library and preserves explicit runtime boundaries.
    </?01M0NJZ4RS2480NMSEN7VBV7BY>
  )>
)>
